201 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(Budi Gunadi Sadikin has served as Indonesia\220s Minister of Health since December 2020. He is a proven public health leader with experience steering reform across the decentralised health system of a large and complex middle-income country, serving more than 280 million people across over 7,000 inhabited islands. Appointed at the height of the COVID-19 pandemic, he led one of the world\220s largest vaccination programmes, which delivered more than 453 million doses nationwide, and transformed the emergency response into a mandate for long-term health-system reform.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

202 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(For nearly six years, he has led a six-pillar national health transformation combining scientific reasoning, financial discipline, political advocacy,  coalition building and delivery at scale, with a consistent focus on prevention, equitable access, system resilience and sustainable national capacity.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

203 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(Internationally, he works across the G20, ASEAN, Gavi, the Stop TB Partnership, TB Vaccine Accelerator Council and the Accra Reset, advancing collective action on pandemic preparedness, sustainable health financing, local production and a more country-led global health architecture.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

204 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(What distinguishes Sadikin is not simply the breadth of his experience, but the consistency of his leadership across sectors. From physics and technology at IBM Asia-Pacific to leading Bank Mandiri and Indonesia\220s state-owned mining holding company, serving as Vice Minister of State-Owned Enterprises and driving national health-system transformation, he has repeatedly demonstrated the same leadership pattern: setting clear direction, aligning diverse interests, mobilizing resources, driving disciplined execution, and delivering at scale.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

