<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 164 0 R/E(Since becoming Indonesia\220s Minister of Health in 2020, Minister Budi has drawn on his experience across health and finance to make sustainable financing an integral part of the country\220s health transformation. Working across government and with development partners, he has translated national health priorities into investment needs and mobilised resources to accelerate transformation at scale.)/Pg 48 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

844 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 164 0 R/E(This approach has helped mobilise US$8.75 billion in external financing, comprising US$3.75 billion in grants and US$5 billion from multilateral development banks. Of the MDB financing, US$4 billion supports a government-led Health Systems Strengthening programme co-financed by the World Bank, ADB, AIIB and IsDB\204the World Bank\220s largest-ever health-sector investment and the largest MDB co-investment in human development. The investment is equipping over 10,000 primary healthcare facilities, 500 public-health laboratories and 600 hospitals with medical equipment, with a particular focus on strengthening cancer, cardiac, stroke and uro-nephrology services.)/Pg 48 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

