912 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 168 0 R/E(Leadership in health requires more than technical expertise. It demands political courage, sound judgement, the ability to mobilise people and resources, and, above all, the determination to translate commitments into results. Minister Budi  embodies these qualities.)/Pg 52 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

913 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 168 0 R/E(Through his leadership of Indonesia\220s health transformation and his contribution to the Accra Reset, I have come to appreciate his ability to approach complex health challenges with clarity, pragmatism and a strong sense of purpose. Having assumed office during the COVID-19 pandemic, he helped steer one of the world\220s largest and most diverse countries through an unprecedented emergency, while using that experience to build a stronger, more equitable and resilient health system.)/Pg 52 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

914 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 168 0 R/E(What distinguishes Minister Sadikin is his combination of public-health leadership, financial acumen and experience in managing large institutions. He understands that sustainable health progress must be nationally owned, adequately financed and supported by strong regional and international cooperation.)/Pg 52 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

915 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 168 0 R/E(At a time when global health faces profound challenges, WHO needs leadership that can listen, build trust across regions and turn collective ambition into practical action. I believe Minister Sadikin possesses the experience, discipline and inclusive leadership required to bring Member States together and help WHO deliver meaningful results for all people.)/Pg 52 0 R/K[4]>>
