2010 0 obj
<</Title(During Indonesia\220s 2022 G20 Presidency, Minister Budi led the health track and worked alongside Indonesia\220s Minister of Finance, Sri Mulyani Indrawati, to bring together health and finance leaders from across the G20. Together, they built consensus across the G20, whose members included several of WHO\220s largest government contributors, on establishing a new fund amid the economic fallout of COVID-19, rising inflation and mounting debt pressures.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2007 0 R/Next 2011 0 R>>
endobj

2011 0 obj
<</Title(That consensus paved the way for the Pandemic Fund, the first multilateral financing mechanism dedicated to providing multiyear grants for pandemic prevention, preparedness and response. The Fund was officially launched in Bali with US$1.4 billion in seed funding committed by 24 donors, including US$50 million from Indonesia. The World Bank recognised the Fund as having been \215developed with Indonesia\220s and Italy\220s leadership during their respective G20 presidencies.\216)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2007 0 R/Prev 2010 0 R>>
